{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion","id":976058,"title":"Technocratic Union annual budget proportion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T12:52:44-07:00","id":976058,"title":"Technocratic Union annual budget proportion","content":"I personally speculate like the below;<br /> <br /> Iteration X : 20%<br /> Progenitors: 20%<br /> New World Order: 20%<br /> Syndicate: Self-sustaining. Though I suspect their internal budget would be smaller than other Conventions.<br /> Void Engineers: 40%<br /> <br /> Have you any idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-04-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:37:43-07:00","id":976075,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that, in the normal sense of allocation of funds, an &quot;annual budget&quot; has any meaning in an organization of mages. Perhaps some things are precious and rate (Quintessence, for example), but, for pretty much anything, ANYTHING, else the right Spheres make the idea a non-issue. <br /> <br /> For Void Engineers, for example, it's like trying down to pin down the budget allocation of Star Fleet in the Star Trek universe, when they have replicators. What CAN'T they make, in abundance, effectively instantly, except for a very very limited set of things. You'd have to track down what actually has value for the VE's. Like ways to avoid Void Adaptation. Shore leave on Earth may be more precious than gold or diamonds (which they can create out of thin air or just transmogrify from the sludge in the sewer tanks). <br /> <br /> For the NWO and Syndicate, influence over mundane institutions or the ability to affect public opinion might be more important than filling up their bank accounts. Sure, the Syndicate is the $$$ Convention, but any reasonably well-staffed NWO Amalgam is going to have as much money as it wants. After all, it's just 1's and 0's in a database. The Spheres needed are pretty much child's play (or low level Disciples' play... maybe even high end Initiates'). <br /> <br /> And so on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:57:44-07:00","id":976082,"title":"","content":"A Post-Scarcity economy would be a fundamental violation of the Paradigm of the Syndicate, so I imagine that they would stomp hard on any Void Engineer attempts to create replicators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:27:06-07:00","id":976155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976075#post976075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that, in the normal sense of allocation of funds, an &quot;annual budget&quot; has any meaning in an organization of mages. Perhaps some things are precious and rate (Quintessence, for example), but, for pretty much anything, ANYTHING, else the right Spheres make the idea a non-issue.<br /> <br /> For Void Engineers, for example, it's like trying down to pin down the budget allocation of Star Fleet in the Star Trek universe, when they have replicators. What CAN'T they make, in abundance, effectively instantly, except for a very very limited set of things. You'd have to track down what actually has value for the VE's. Like ways to avoid Void Adaptation. Shore leave on Earth may be more precious than gold or diamonds (which they can create out of thin air or just transmogrify from the sludge in the sewer tanks).<br /> <br /> For the NWO and Syndicate, influence over mundane institutions or the ability to affect public opinion might be more important than filling up their bank accounts. Sure, the Syndicate is the $$$ Convention, but any reasonably well-staffed NWO Amalgam is going to have as much money as it wants. After all, it's just 1's and 0's in a database. The Spheres needed are pretty much child's play (or low level Disciples' play... maybe even high end Initiates').<br /> <br /> And so on...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Enlightened Science etc. seems to take care of a lot of goods - superficially. They actually don't.<br /> <br /> Star Trek has replicators, but those replicators need feedstock. Mass-energy or elements. Voidy replicators aren't going to bypass that, even if they use Quintessence as fuel instead.<br /> <br /> For the rest of it, when not using public Devices, the cost isn't that of the good so much as it is the <i>service</i> that it entails. Indeed, apart from Primal Energy and Wonders, the Union's internal markets likely consist almost entirely of services offered and the products thereof. Clone personnel? Someone either spent Automated Cloning Vat time or had a Master-level Life Scientist making the body, and a Master-level Mind Scientist making the psyche. A shiny new Micro Tool Kit? Same deal, if not as <i>much</i> cost. Need a media campaign manufactured? Even if you don't use Enlightened support for that, you're asking a lot of people to use their time, effort, and resources to make it happen.<br /> <br /> And all that can be numericised, codified, and formalized into an enumeration of value. In other words? <i>Money</i>. Meaning, this is something that the Syndicate has been doing since the Order of Reason if not earlier.<br /> <br /> When you allocate an amount of Prime and Service that a group has to work with, that's a budget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:11:22-07:00","id":976250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976075#post976075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that, in the normal sense of allocation of funds, an &quot;annual budget&quot; has any meaning in an organization of mages. Perhaps some things are precious and rate (Quintessence, for example), but, for pretty much anything, ANYTHING, else the right Spheres make the idea a non-issue.<br /> <br /> For Void Engineers, for example, it's like trying down to pin down the budget allocation of Star Fleet in the Star Trek universe, when they have replicators. What CAN'T they make, in abundance, effectively instantly, except for a very very limited set of things. You'd have to track down what actually has value for the VE's. Like ways to avoid Void Adaptation. Shore leave on Earth may be more precious than gold or diamonds (which they can create out of thin air or just transmogrify from the sludge in the sewer tanks).<br /> <br /> For the NWO and Syndicate, influence over mundane institutions or the ability to affect public opinion might be more important than filling up their bank accounts. Sure, the Syndicate is the $$$ Convention, but any reasonably well-staffed NWO Amalgam is going to have as much money as it wants. After all, it's just 1's and 0's in a database. The Spheres needed are pretty much child's play (or low level Disciples' play... maybe even high end Initiates').<br /> <br /> And so on...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Syndicate has no use to the Union whatsoever. In other words, you are portraying them fundamentally redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:17:32-07:00","id":976256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976082#post976082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Post-Scarcity economy would be a fundamental violation of the Paradigm of the Syndicate, so I imagine that they would stomp hard on any Void Engineer attempts to create replicators.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. The Syndicate's stated end goal IS a global post-scarcity economy. That is the reason why they have conducted so many Utopia experiments throughout its long history, and each and all of these are invariably failed due to Unbelief of the Masses. So with a resigned, exasperated sigh, they finally invented and created modern capitalist economy - aka. Status Quo. Not because they WANT it, but because they could not find any other viable option.<br /> <br /> And the Voidies DO have and use <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">replicators. That is one of the example Devises. And hell, those are not your normal nano replicators, but <i>femto </i>replicators. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:37:30-07:00","id":976268,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity, where does it say that the Convention of cash wants a post-scarcity society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:55:39-07:00","id":976285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976268#post976268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, where does it say that the Convention of cash wants a post-scarcity society?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate, and their predecessor the High Guild, has always aspired <b><i>cashless </i></b>society. That has been explicitly elaborated from the First Edition, when the Technocracy was portrayed as mustache-twirling comic book villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:09:33-07:00","id":976296,"title":"","content":"Cashless societies are not the same as post-scarcity societies. A world with a digital currency is a cashless society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:13:33-07:00","id":976300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976155#post976155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all that can be numericised, codified, and formalized into an enumeration of value. In other words? <i>Money</i>. Meaning, this is something that the Syndicate has been doing since the Order of Reason if not earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> And in my games, the Syndicate's greatest trick was, during the creation of Bretton Woods, pegging Primal Energy -- the one resource precious enough to Technocrats to be considered currency in and of itself -- to the USD, which in turn allowed exchange, speculation, market derivatives, and the like. And, providing a much-needed check and balance with the rest of the Technocratic Union to keep them from fucking with currency values, precious resource supply, and money supply outside the purview of the Timeline, lest they chop off their own heads in the process. The Nixon shock was sold to the other Conventions as the first major &quot;market correction&quot; of the postwar era, but was in reality a major coup on the Syndicate's part to eliminate other Conventions' ability to undermine Syndicate control of resources, resource production, and independent exchange of PE. The advent of Primal Utility, and the free exchange between Primal Energy and Sleeper currency, is the first step in the Syndicate's endgame to perform a hostile takeover of the Technocratic Union itself.<br /> <br /> Not that, in my games, the NWO is taking this laying down. The NWO likes oil, and they <i>really</i> like authoritarian regimes in control of oil-rich countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:59:42-07:00","id":976550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976155#post976155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Enlightened Science etc. seems to take care of a lot of goods - superficially. They actually don't.<br /> <br /> Star Trek has replicators, but those replicators need feedstock. Mass-energy or elements. Voidy replicators aren't going to bypass that, even if they use Quintessence as fuel instead.<br /> <br /> For the rest of it, when not using public Devices, the cost isn't that of the good so much as it is the <i>service</i> that it entails. Indeed, apart from Primal Energy and Wonders, the Union's internal markets likely consist almost entirely of services offered and the products thereof. Clone personnel? Someone either spent Automated Cloning Vat time or had a Master-level Life Scientist making the body, and a Master-level Mind Scientist making the psyche. A shiny new Micro Tool Kit? Same deal, if not as <i>much</i> cost. Need a media campaign manufactured? Even if you don't use Enlightened support for that, you're asking a lot of people to use their time, effort, and resources to make it happen.<br /> <br /> And all that can be numericised, codified, and formalized into an enumeration of value. In other words? <i>Money</i>. Meaning, this is something that the Syndicate has been doing since the Order of Reason if not earlier.<br /> <br /> When you allocate an amount of Prime and Service that a group has to work with, that's a budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a budget, but it's not quantifiable in terms of %'s of total, as the various parts of the economy in play are fundamentally different from each other. Quintessence alone demonstrates how complex the web is. Sure, the Syndicate is effectively rolling in the stuff. Primal Utility and a world full of ventures pretty much sets that up. So, sure, the Syndicate can allocate the Quint produced in accordance with the directives of Control and the demands of the Timeline. However, that's a very superficial way to look at how it's going to go. Some ventures are going to be specifically tasked to the needs of an Amalgam. Some are going to be self-feeding the Amalgam they are in, even if it is multi-Convention. Some are producing Quint &quot;cash&quot; and spreading it around. And that doesn't begin to address the complications the Nodes bring into play, as some Amalgams from other Conventions don't even enter the Syndicate's system of exchange. Maybe the VE's are tossing BEM's and PLE's into engines and converting all that Gnosis into usable Prime energy? Sure, the Syndicate is going to supply a lot of the Quint to produce a lot of the Devices in play, particularly if they are mass-produced or they are HUGELY expensive (like a Void Ship), but it's not a simple system at all. It's going to take a lot of high level math to manage.<br /> <br /> And that's just ONE thing. The Syndicate isn't stupid enough to just slap a price tag on a service. The Syndicate deals more in <i>value </i>than in price. Some services are worth more in some circumstances than others. Ideas of &quot;money&quot; change, but the concept of value applies back to the days of the High Guild (which is interpreted in terms of modern economics, but that's a completely flawed paradigm for pre-Industrial societies... back to the Renaissance it works to a degree, but the idea of Medieval &quot;trade&quot; just doesn't describe what went on.... and before that. it's just plain wrong) and it will continue to apply on to Economics 2.0 (post-scarcity, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 09-26-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:39:26-07:00","id":976713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976296#post976296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cashless societies are not the same as post-scarcity societies. A world with a digital currency is a cashless society.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Cashless society is not a post scarcity society.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a cashless society.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2016/jun/04/sweden-cashless-society-cards-phone-apps-leading-europe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/b18accb34d6bae5726851afa33fa3fa8524d530a/0_269_4096_2458/4096.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdG8tYWdlLTIwMTYucG5n&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=49958298e49c6a1da28521d40e81083b\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2016/jun/04/sweden-cashless-society-cards-phone-apps-leading-europe\" target=\"_blank\"> Sweden leads the race to become cashless society </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2016/jun/04/sweden-cashless-society-cards-phone-apps-leading-europe\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.theguardian.com/business/2016/jun/04/sweden-cashless-society-cards-phone-apps-leading-europe </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Swedes are blazing a trail in Europe, with banks, buses, street vendors and even churches expecting plastic or virtual payment </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:34:15-07:00","id":976917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976550#post976550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a budget, but it's not quantifiable in terms of %'s of total, as the various parts of the economy in play are fundamentally different from each other. Quintessence alone demonstrates how complex the web is. Sure, the Syndicate is effectively rolling in the stuff. Primal Utility and a world full of ventures pretty much sets that up. So, sure, the Syndicate can allocate the Quint produced in accordance with the directives of Control and the demands of the Timeline. However, that's a very superficial way to look at how it's going to go. Some ventures are going to be specifically tasked to the needs of an Amalgam. Some are going to be self-feeding the Amalgam they are in, even if it is multi-Convention. Some are producing Quint &quot;cash&quot; and spreading it around. And that doesn't begin to address the complications the Nodes bring into play, as some Amalgams from other Conventions don't even enter the Syndicate's system of exchange. Maybe the VE's are tossing BEM's and PLE's into engines and converting all that Gnosis into usable Prime energy? Sure, the Syndicate is going to supply a lot of the Quint to produce a lot of the Devices in play, particularly if they are mass-produced or they are HUGELY expensive (like a Void Ship), but it's not a simple system at all. It's going to take a lot of high level math to manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not under any sort of misconception that the Syndicate is the Union's sole source of Primal Energy. All that means, though, is that the Conventions' respective budgets are larger than Disbursements' &quot;how much to allocate to each project&quot; budget. Likewise, the budgets for individual Amalgams etc. who have their own Nodes are consequently going to account for having that Node. And so on.<br /> <br /> As for the mathematical difficulties and masses of variables entailed... gee. It's almost as if people who can use Iteration X-sourced computing systems to model and predict complex systems might be useful to the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> <b>Budgeting (Time 2/Entropy 4/Primal Utility 1)</b><br /> <br /> By using advanced predictive algorithms, reams of financial data, and intuitive estimations, the Syndic can model the known sources of revenue and expenditures of an organization, acquiring a comprehensive overview of its financial status. Furthermore, by applying this knowledge in financial planning, they can ensure that the organization wastes as little of their available resources as possible.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Time 2/Primal Utility 1/Entropy 1 acquires an estimate of the target organization's most likely expenditures, whether in dollars, Primal Energy, or some other abstract measure of value. Entropy 4 blesses the organization via subtle shifts and optimizations to prevent misfortune from causing them to go 'over budget'.<br /> <br /> This rote is also used by the Time-Motion Managers, and to some extent the Ivory Tower and occasional members of other Conventions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's just ONE thing. The Syndicate isn't stupid enough to just slap a price tag on a service. The Syndicate deals more in <i>value </i>than in price. Some services are worth more in some circumstances than others. Ideas of &quot;money&quot; change, but the concept of value applies back to the days of the High Guild (which is interpreted in terms of modern economics, but that's a completely flawed paradigm for pre-Industrial societies... back to the Renaissance it works to a degree, but the idea of Medieval &quot;trade&quot; just doesn't describe what went on.... and before that. it's just plain wrong) and it will continue to apply on to Economics 2.0 (post-scarcity, etc.). </div> </div> </div>Um.<br /> <br /> Okay, this seems rather bizarre to hear from you. Of <i>course</i> the Syndicate aren't blithering idiots who try to impose from on high the prices of all things. That sort of silliness is the NWO's schtick, what with the central planning and publicly held institutions and whatnot. The Invisible Hand of the Market - i.e., Consensus - is what determines prices, not the Syndicate bigwigs in their glass-and-concrete towers.<br /> <br /> The budget is an estimate of how much the group in question has to work with, and money is an approximation of value. Those estimates and approximations aren't 100% perfectly precise and accurate. That's what makes them estimates and approximations; they're still useful, in much the same way as knowing <i>approximately</i> how much an object weighs is useful for determining whether you can fit it on an elevator without going over the load limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:45:14-07:00","id":977049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976296#post976296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cashless societies are not the same as post-scarcity societies. A world with a digital currency is a cashless society.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cashless economy is just a step to the post-scarcity society. The Syndicate sincerely aspires post-scarcity society. However the Masses has rejected their every attempt of the Utopian social engineering, denied their every clarion offer to the peace and prosperity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:34:21-07:00","id":977170,"title":"","content":"I do not think that the Syndicate is actually going for anything more sophisticated than a cashless society where they can arbitrarily manipulate the value of everything from coffee to water. Honestly, I think that the NWO seems more interested in Utopian fantasies than the Syndicate, as almost every Utopian society ends up as a fascist society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:23:33-07:00","id":977395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=977170#post977170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I as almost every Utopian society ends up as a fascist society.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very bold statement that really needs to be supported and not just thrown out there for it's value of truth. Proof please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:39:51-07:00","id":977407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=976917#post976917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um.<br /> <br /> Okay, this seems rather bizarre to hear from you. Of <i>course</i> the Syndicate aren't blithering idiots who try to impose from on high the prices of all things. That sort of silliness is the NWO's schtick, what with the central planning and publicly held institutions and whatnot. The Invisible Hand of the Market - i.e., Consensus - is what determines prices, not the Syndicate bigwigs in their glass-and-concrete towers.<br /> <br /> The budget is an estimate of how much the group in question has to work with, and money is an approximation of value. Those estimates and approximations aren't 100% perfectly precise and accurate. That's what makes them estimates and approximations; they're still useful, in much the same way as knowing <i>approximately</i> how much an object weighs is useful for determining whether you can fit it on an elevator without going over the load limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Okay, I'll take that. It was really bizarre in retrospect. I was multi-tasking out the wazzo while trying to finish it up and it was garbled at best. <br /> <br /> However, I don't accept that identifying and managing the &quot;market&quot; is a NWO thing. Nor that what the NWO does is in any way silliness. In fact, I would hold out that the Syndicate can't exist AT ALL without the NWO with respect to the Masses. To have a market, you need an economy. To have an economy on a scale past central resource re-allocation (i.e. the so-called &quot;Big Man&quot; system), you have to have a state-level government. And government is the NWO's thing. It's really hard to keep track of the &quot;who is richest&quot; game if there isn't such a thing as &quot;money&quot; and guess who defines what that is? You can't have markets without states, but you sure as hell can have states without markets. Vide pretty much all of history and prehistory for examples galore. <br /> <br /> Sometimes the NWO manages the market, but most often it leaves that entirely to the Syndicate as that is what the Syndicate does and isn't really what the NWO does . Sometimes it subordinates it to government completely a la Diocletion-esque price-fixing. Sometimes, the Syndicate is allowed to run amok with very little to no integration with larger issues (and, yes, there are larger issues than economics, economists egos notwithstanding). Currently, the two Conventions seems to have come to some kind of detente where they are both working in tandem while competing for influence. Not so long ago, the Syndicate and the NWO were trying this combo out over here, this other variant over there the NWO was trying out some stuff with little to no Syndicate involved at all. <br /> <br /> Irrespective of the NWO and the Syndicate vis-a-vis the Masses, the Syndicate has a particular job within the Union (that of tracking resource allocation) and the NWO has another job (control of information). Neither has the job of &quot;Being in Charge&quot;. That's Control. <br /> <br /> But I really doubt that with Entropy 4 and 5 available as well as Time 2 and up, the Syndicate is sitting down and preparing budget as per an accounting firm. They are able to things that people in those feels slaver over, but just aren't possible with anything we have now (except playing finance games, e.g. cheating and lying): Real-time plan-scoping. Projective analyses concerning variable resource exchange management. Holistic inclusion of exernalites in cost management. Risk assessment without any need for risk or assessment. Etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:52:40-07:00","id":977413,"title":"","content":"Admittedly I was a bit more unclear than advisable for the sake of being a bit more IC-ish; from the Syndicate's perspective, the NWO is probably silly/wrongheaded for doing centralized planning for things in general. It was more a commentary on how the modern capitalist Syndicate doesn't really do centralized control as a thing, and that would necessarily entail them not doing price-fixing. The noo-woos have their reasons for what they do, and they're not unreasonable ones.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the NWO's jurisdiction doesn't actually entail managing economies, you're right there. Didn't mean to imply otherwise if I did so.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=977407#post977407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I really doubt that with Entropy 4 and 5 available as well as Time 2 and up, the Syndicate is sitting down and preparing budget as per an accounting firm. They are able to things that people in those feels slaver over, but just aren't possible with anything we have now (except playing finance games, e.g. cheating and lying): Real-time plan-scoping. Projective analyses concerning variable resource exchange management. Holistic inclusion of exernalites in cost management. Risk assessment without any need for risk or assessment. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, maybe I have an erroneously over-generalized idea of what 'making a budget' entails? Possible, at least.<br /> <br /> The basic question I'm reading in the OP of &quot;how much of the Union's overall resources, as a rule-of-thumb figure, do each of the Conventions use up&quot; still seems valid as a thing you could plausibly estimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:39:02-07:00","id":977516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=977413#post977413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The basic question I'm reading in the OP of &quot;how much of the Union's overall resources, as a rule-of-thumb figure, do each of the Conventions use up&quot; still seems valid as a thing you could plausibly estimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it looks something like this:<br /> <br /> Iteration X 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks)<br /> NWO 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks, and we almost certainly are)<br /> Progenitors 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks)<br /> Syndicate 100% of what we need + what we can chisel out of the others just 'cause it makes us look more badass<br /> Void Engineers What the Hell do these guys DO anyways and what do they need it for?... Hmmmm...... Given 'em 50%<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:59:25-07:00","id":977553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=977516#post977516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it looks something like this:<br /> <br /> Iteration X 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks)<br /> NWO 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks, and we almost certainly are)<br /> Progenitors 100% of what they need that they can't produce for themselves (unless we - the Syndicate, are being dicks)<br /> Syndicate 100% of what we need + what we can chisel out of the others just 'cause it makes us look more badass<br /> Void Engineers What the Hell do these guys DO anyways and what do they need it for?... Hmmmm...... Given 'em 50%</div> </div> </div> </div>...Okay, fine. You don't think it's a meaningful topic, I get it. :/<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> To the OP, I'd probably say the Void Engineers' official budget is becoming more and more constrained over time due to backlash from the other Conventions, though Disbursements <i>does</i> handle the Syndicate's internal revenues so they'd probably have an amount pegged for that too. I'd imagine there'd be bias towards allocations toward Syndicate matters just because that sort of bias is part of human nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-28-2016, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:09:54-07:00","id":977852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976058-technocratic-union-annual-budget-proportion?p=977553#post977553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Okay, fine. You don't think it's a meaningful topic, I get it. :/<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> To the OP, I'd probably say the Void Engineers' official budget is becoming more and more constrained over time due to backlash from the other Conventions, though Disbursements <i>does</i> handle the Syndicate's internal revenues so they'd probably have an amount pegged for that too. I'd imagine there'd be bias towards allocations toward Syndicate matters just because that sort of bias is part of human nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I think it's a fine topic. But I think that the terms have to be defined. To say X% here, Y% there, and so on, until it all adds up to 100% doesn't work. Or, it gives such a superficial gloss on the situation that it is nigh meaningless. <br /> <br /> &quot;Budgeting&quot; the Technocracy like trying to map a post-scarcity economy, overlaid with a distribution network for extremely rare resources, in tandem with a quid-pro-quo service exchange scheme, all within a set of functional guidelines concerning the overall mission statement (which isn't just propaganda, though it is that too, but it's also a matrix into which this &quot;budget&quot; and many, many other things are fit) and trying to put that on the balance sheet. It doesn't work. No matter how n-dimensional your pivot tables are. <br /> <br /> You need to break the fundamentals down. <br /> <br /> That's where the &quot;100% funded&quot; comes in. It demonstrates the &quot;post-scarcity&quot; nature of trying to grasp allocation of almost all of what we would call resources across the Union. It also takes in your &quot;bias of human nature&quot; comes in. And it does address the issue with mages being able to just create almost everything they need from &quot;thin air&quot; using elementary applications of Spheres. <br /> <br /> It doesn't address the whole idea of the exchange/distribution of &quot;ultra-rare&quot; commodities, like Quintessence or Devices. That's a whole different model. Hells, it might be more like the kula ring exchange in Melanesia than it is like a market economy. Or a top-down &quot;Big Man&quot; system. (Though those two do cross over). In which case, a &quot;budget&quot; model is for crap. Or it's like a complicated pre-market distribution network, as per, say, the way the Pharoahs managed the econimics/subsistence of Ancient Egypt. It's a lock it's not like what we've got going on. <br /> <br /> And budget models are always for crap when trying to get a handle on service exchange networks. We just can't seem to really monetize such exchanges in any comprehensive way as you are always moving from one paradigm to another when you do so. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}